From: pixel2 ubuntu port
Subject: [PATCH] venus: msm8998: no recovery after a firmware crash

On msm8998 the venus firmware comes up once per boot: Porthole's 0198
found that no path back from a firmware shutdown works. The system
error handler still tried, five times (shutdown, PAS boot, HFI init),
and a crash during an encode was followed by a SoC reset some seconds
after it gave up (pixel2 tests 56 and 78).

Skip the recovery on 3xx. sys_error stays set and the IRQ stays off,
so every HFI entry point fails cleanly and the codec is unavailable
until the next boot.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -141,6 +141,19 @@
 	const char *err_msg = "";
 	bool failed = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * msm8998: the firmware comes up only once per boot (no restart after
+	 * a shutdown, see venus_probe), and the recovery attempt is followed
+	 * by a SoC reset. Leave the dead core alone instead: sys_error stays
+	 * set and the IRQ off, so every HFI entry point fails cleanly and the
+	 * codec is gone until the next boot, but the system stays up.
+	 */
+	if (IS_V3(core)) {
+		dev_err(core->dev,
+			"firmware crashed, video codec unavailable until reboot\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(core->dev);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		err_msg = "resume runtime PM";
